From: nemo-speech-python
Subject: ggml-cpu: check AVX512-VBMI in the score of MSVC variants

With MSVC, the AVX512-VBMI variants (cannonlake, icelake) define only
__AVX512VBMI__, not GGML_AVX512_VBMI, which the feature check of
ggml_backend_score() tests. Their score then equals that of the variants
without VBMI (skylakex, cascadelake), and the tie goes to the first file
name: cannonlake on a Skylake-X, cascadelake on an Ice Lake. The code does
not use VBMI on MSVC, so nothing crashes, but the selection and the
reported features are wrong. Define GGML_AVX512_VBMI as GCC builds do.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
index 1c7338e..a49ad05 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ function(ggml_add_cpu_backend_variant_impl tag_name)
                 # Do it manually.
                 list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS GGML_AVX512)
                 if (GGML_AVX512_VBMI)
-                    list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS __AVX512VBMI__)
+                    list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS __AVX512VBMI__ GGML_AVX512_VBMI)
                     if (CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "Clang")
                         list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS -mavx512vbmi)
                     endif()
